35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The audit revealed a painful truth: hardware requires outside appraisals, adding six weeks and significant fees. This directly impacts our quarter-end clarity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The data confirms my suspicion. Our profitable exits were quiet back-office tools. The write-off ran physical premises. We should avoid operational complexity.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,The credit line ignores subscription contracts. Reserves are drained by equipment-heavy holdings. We need a software model to protect our liquidity.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, recruiters can't find shift supervisors or field crews fast enough! But we have three logistics advisers sitting idle. That’s a huge gap!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The data is clear. Medical and financial records add three quarters to deployment. Hardware caused five months of delay. Software never missed a release.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Minako, your liquidity concern is valid. Yet, if we choose software, we lose the independent verification I seek. We must balance both.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, that is a false dilemma. The back-office tooling we exited was software, yet it was bought by an incumbent. We need to verify the actual retention, not just the asset class.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Servas, I hear you, but the credit line treats subscriptions as worthless. If we pick hardware, we cannot borrow against it. We must prioritize liquidity.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, your delay data is scary! But @Asuka, if we pick software, we avoid those long searches. I’m leaning toward the dashboard idea!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the dashboard idea fits. No hardware, no external dependencies. The bank tool proved that software deploys on schedule.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, you are right. Verification is not exclusive to hardware. I seek a model where our own records remain auditable without external appraisals.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, exactly. The shopkeeper tool lost a third of accounts, proving software isn't automatically safe. We need the specific retention data to distinguish the winners from the losers.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, retention is vital, but liquidity is survival. If the credit line won't back subscriptions, we need a model that doesn't drain our reserves.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, that retention data is key! If the clinic software keeps its users, it solves my hiring worries too. I’m definitely leaning that way!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, retention is the final test. The bank tool proved delivery, but only sustained usage proves the product sticks. I need that confirmation.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, I agree. We must find a model that is both liquid and verifiable. Let us await the candidates to test these criteria.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
